### Chart Colors
For data visualization (playful rotation):
- `--chart-1` (violet) through `--chart-5` (blue)

## Decision Flow

### When Styling a Component:

1. **First, check if a semantic variable exists:**
   ```tsx
   // ✅ CORRECT - Uses semantic variable
   <div className="bg-background text-foreground">
   
   // ❌ WRONG - Hardcoded color
   <div className="bg-[#F9FAFB] text-[#1a1a1a]">
   ```

2. **If no semantic variable fits, check if a playful palette color works:**
   ```tsx
   // ✅ CORRECT - Uses playful palette
   <div className="bg-tertiary text-tertiary-foreground">
   
   // ❌ WRONG - Arbitrary color
   <div className="bg-[#FBBF24]">
   ```

3. **If a new color is truly needed, ADD IT TO `app/app.css` first:**
   ```css
   /* In :root section of app/app.css */
   --new-color: #HEX;
   --new-color-foreground: #HEX;
   ```
   
   Then register it in the `@theme inline` block:
   ```css
   @theme inline {
     --color-new-color: var(--new-color);
     --color-new-color-foreground: var(--new-color-foreground);
   }
   ```

4. **For dark mode support, also add to `.dark` section**

## Forbidden Patterns

### ❌ Never Use Template Literals for Class Names
```tsx
// BAD
<div className={`p-4 ${isActive ? "bg-primary" : ""} ${className}`}>

// GOOD
<div className={cn("p-4", isActive && "bg-primary", className)}>
```

### ❌ Never Use Hardcoded Colors in Classes
```tsx
// BAD
<div className="bg-[#003362]">
<div className="text-[rgb(100,100,100)]">

// GOOD - Use semantic variables
<div className="bg-primary">
```

### ❌ Never Use Tailwind's Default Palette for Semantic UI
```tsx
// BAD
<button className="bg-blue-600 text-white">

// GOOD
<button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
```

### ❌ Never Use Soft Blurred Shadows
```tsx
// BAD - Soft shadows don't fit this design system
<div className="shadow-lg">
<div className="shadow-md">

// GOOD - Hard pop shadows
<div className="shadow-pop">
<div className="shadow-pop-lg">
```

### ❌ Never Use Small Border Radii for Visible Containers
```tsx
// BAD - Too subtle
<div className="rounded-sm">
<div className="rounded-md">

// GOOD - Bold geometric shapes
<div className="rounded-xl">
<div className="rounded-full">
```

