## Playful Geometric Design Patterns

### Card Components ("Sticker Cards")
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Playful card with hard shadow and wiggle
<div className="rounded-xl border-2 border-border-strong bg-card p-6 shadow-pop-muted hover:rotate-[-1deg] hover:scale-[1.02] transition-all duration-300">

// For featured cards, use colored shadows:
<div className="rounded-xl border-2 border-border-strong bg-card p-6 shadow-pop-pink">

// ❌ WRONG - Soft organic styling
<div className="rounded-[24px] border-border/30 bg-card p-8 shadow-warm">
```

### Buttons ("Candy Buttons")
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Primary candy button
<Button>Get Started</Button>  // Default variant already styled

// ✅ CORRECT - Outline with yellow hover fill
<Button variant="outline">Learn More</Button>

// ❌ WRONG - Soft organic styling
<Button className="rounded-[16px] shadow-warm">Submit</Button>
```

### Inputs (Hard Shadow Focus)
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Input with chunky border and pop shadow on focus
<Input placeholder="Enter your name" />  // Default already styled

// ❌ WRONG
<input className="rounded-md border shadow-xs">
```

### Decorative Elements
```tsx
// ✅ Floating shape behind content
<div className="absolute -top-4 -right-4 w-16 h-16 rounded-full bg-tertiary animate-float" />

// ✅ Icon enclosed in a colored circle
<div className="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-quaternary">
  <CheckIcon className="text-white" strokeWidth={2.5} />
</div>

// ✅ Dot grid background pattern
<section className="bg-dot-grid py-24">
```

### Animations
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Bouncy pop-in entrance
<div className="animate-pop-in">First element</div>
<div className="animate-pop-in-delay-200">Second element</div>

// ✅ CORRECT - Wiggle on hover for icons
<div className="hover:animate-wiggle">🎉</div>
```

### Iconography (Lucide React)
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Bold chunky icons enclosed in shapes
<CheckIcon strokeWidth={2.5} className="text-white" />

// Icons should be enclosed in colored circles:
<div className="flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary">
  <StarIcon strokeWidth={2.5} className="size-4 text-white" />
</div>

// ❌ WRONG - Floating icon alone
<StarIcon className="text-gray-500" />
```

## Adding New CSS Variables

When you need a color that doesn't exist:

1. **Name it semantically** (by purpose, not by color):
   - ✅ `--success`, `--warning`, `--info`
   - ❌ `--green`, `--yellow`, `--blue-light`

2. **Use hex color format** for consistency with existing variables:
   ```css
   --new-color: #HEX;
   ```

3. **Always define both light and dark variants** in their respective sections

4. **Register in `@theme inline`** to make it available as a Tailwind class

## File Reference
- **CSS Variables Location:** `app/app.css`
- **Light mode variables:** `:root { ... }`
- **Dark mode variables:** `.dark { ... }`
- **Tailwind theme mapping:** `@theme inline { ... }`
